<title>SOUTH AFRICA: AROMA SAYS LIQUOR STOCKS OVERSTATED.</title>
<headline>AROMA SAYS LIQUOR STOCKS OVERSTATED.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aroma Liquor Holdings said on Friday that in annual results to February which were published in May, an error had been discovered in the valuation of bonded liquor stocks.</p>
<p>As a result income attributable to shareholders should have been stated at 519,000 or 3.2 cents a share instead of 1.129 million rand, equivalent to seven cents a share.</p>
<p>The company said the error would be corrected when it published its results for the sixteen months to June in August.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
